; DOMAIN: geometry/ricci-flow-entropy-monotonicity [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-26]
; Claim: Perelman's F- and W-entropies make Ricci flow a gradient flow with monotone entropy, unifying it with thermodynamic and Wasserstein dissipation. (1) F(g,f)=int (R+|grad f|^2) e^{-f} dV is monotone nondecreasing under Ricci flow coupled to backward heat, dF/dt=2 int |Ric+Hess f|^2 e^{-f}>=0; Ricci flow = gradient flow of F. (2) W(g,f,tau)=int [tau(R+|grad f|^2)+f-n](4pi tau)^{-n/2}e^{-f}dV is monotone, dW/dt=2tau int |Ric+Hess f-g/2tau|^2 (...)>=0; shrinking solitons are its critical points. (3) The no-local-collapsing theorem follows from W-monotonicity, ruling out cusp singularities. (4) W is a Boltzmann-type entropy; its monotonicity is the second law for the coupled geometry-diffusion system.
; Structure: (F=int(R+|grad f|^2)e^{-f}dV, dF/dt=2int|Ric+Hess f|^2 e^{-f}>=0) (W with tau, dW/dt>=0, critical=shrinking soliton) (no-local-collapsing from W) (W = Boltzmann entropy => 2nd-law reading).
; Result: Ricci flow is an entropy-driven gradient descent: Perelman's monotone F/W entropies play the role of a Lyapunov functional, identifying solitons as fixed points and forbidding collapse, exactly parallel to free-energy dissipation in diffusion.
; Bridge: genesis_ricci_flow (Perelman F/W are the Lyapunov functionals proving Ricci flow is a gradient flow; solitons=critical points refine the flow node's fixed-point picture) + genesis_wasserstein_gradient_flow_JKO (W-entropy monotonicity is the geometric analogue of F(rho) dissipation along W2 gradient flow; both are entropy-decreasing/increasing minimizing movements) + genesis_thermodynamics_maxent (W is a Boltzmann-Gibbs entropy and its monotonicity is a second-law statement for the coupled geometry+backward-heat system) + genesis_bakry_emery_gamma_calculus (the integrand |Ric+Hess f|^2 is the Bochner/Gamma_2 defect; CD(K,N) and Perelman entropy share the same Ric+Hess f curvature-dimension object).